From 3de82c3454dff5f6e90bc3d400598ceb7a9eedbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:37:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Speak English on a console not set to Spanish

Canica's own words in the menu were Spanish literals, because the
firmware's translation catalogues cannot carry new strings. They now
follow system.language: Spanish when it is es or es_*, English on any
other console (CanicaText.h, read at every use, so a changed language
applies without a stale cache).

That covers START > Canica (its entries, the update modes and the
update row, which takes the updater's detail_en in English), the
activity page (labels, weekdays, the 7-day list, thousands as 12,345),
the game switcher's dates and auto-save line, the Continue collection's
name, the update terminal's percent and a screenshot's date
(month/day/year in English). A Spanish console reads exactly what it
read before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
